WEBVTT

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.070
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.780
<b>June 13, 1582 {yellow ts}</b>

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.780
<b>Owari Province Narumi {ts}</b>

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.120
I bring word from a ferryman near the border of Kyoto!

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.960
General Hashiba joins with Lord Nobutaka
 and General Niwa,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.960
and commands a combined force of 40,000!

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.330
General Akechi...

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.980
<b>A Sorrowful Midnight Purple{ts}</b>

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.410
Should General Akechi be forced to retreat from Oyamazaki

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.290
and flee to his garrison at Shouryuuji Castle,
he shall be besieged.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.770
Without the aid of the Hosokawas,
ensured is the defeat of General Akechi.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.880
The force General Hashiba commands overwhelms.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.000
Not even the likes of Shibata Katsuie may instill such fear.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.700
General Hashiba shall rule almighty over the realm...

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.770
Justice mayn't see defeat.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.850
Milord, there remains no purpose to assist General Akechi.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.820
I advise our return to Mikawa, and subjugation of the Kai and Shinano provinces

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.560
as a means to reinforce our borders from foes.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.900
General Akechi be a true warrior.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.370
Known to him is the fate of defeated rebels.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:01.450
A true warrior, General Akechi is not!

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.740
He be a hero, who rebels for the people!

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.570
The realm requires such a hero to maintain peace!

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.980
Generals, ye may remain here!

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.050
Hanzo, we ride!

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.820
Milord!

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.300
Does Milord relinquish the memory of defeat at Mikatagahara?!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.870
<b>June 13, 1582 {green ts}</b>

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.870
<b>Yamashiro Province Shouryuuji Castle {ts}</b>

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:50.420
Hashiba's forces now surround the castle's entirety.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.730
We few of 100 who remain shall hold their advance.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.610
I am defeated.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.230
Take our remaining men and flee,

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.250
for I desire no other be taken by Death.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.280
Go. {yuke}

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.470
Forsake us not as those who have left Milord.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.860
Milord, we ask of ye to flee.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.750
That which remains in the granary was discarded by fleeing men.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.000
A knot of rope and some miso.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.540
Then all is well!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.380
Defeat hunger, and ye shall conquer men!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:19.500
Hither travel into the presence of Death, then shall ye know the virtues of imperfection.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.770
'Tis a most modest meal, aye?

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.160
Denounce not modesty.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.340
Recall I do of such bounty as a footman.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.360
Joyous days. {mata ikkyou}

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.360
Hold for a moment.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.190
Now, we may feast.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.880
'Tis a bounty of luxury!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:17.190
Fathom I mayn't how a bellflower and pebble-rest may improve such a meal so!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.260
'Tis sweet broth.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:32.190
'Twas not the honey of the flower, but sweetness mine soul feels.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.220
Master Senno...

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.200
I savor as ye do, the virtues of imperfection.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.320
Beauty is indeed eternal...

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.310
Strength does it impart, akin to war...

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.220
Milord.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.610
Messengers of Mt. Hiei request an audience.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.900
What business have ye with a defeated man?

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:19.110
General Hashiba requests of ye to surrender.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.620
Surrender, I shan't.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:28.670
'Twas by your hand that Oda Nobunaga, foe to the Buddha, has perished. {until dekimasenu}

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.490
Such a man we cannot forsake. {until ikinagara he}

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:34.640
We ask ye to accompany us to Enryaku Temple,
 where ye may assist in its restoration.

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:42.760
The destruction of Enryaku Temple was not solely the doing of Oda.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.030
Am I not a foe of the Buddha for partaking?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:50.490
'Twas not a decision ye made of will.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:55.700
Now, Hashiba's forces make their advance on Sakamoto Castle.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.540
Enryaku Temple remains your sole haven.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.620
Make your decision.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.570
Should a defeated rebel suffice

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:15.050
use my talents as ye see fit.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.900
Of course, that is assuming we survive the journey...

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.270
<b>June 14, 1582 {blue ts}</b>

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.270
<b>Omi Province Sakamoto Castle {ts}</b>

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:33.360
We set out with reinforcements from Azuchi to assist Milord...

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.470
only to be besieged in Sakamoto Castle.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.860
So, mine life shall end here...

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.820
General, let Death take us and the castle as well!

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:51.770
I wish not to allow Hashiba to use the cherished castle of Milord!

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:57.220
As wife to Milord, I have but a single request.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.060
Spare the masterpieces.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.710
'Twas the masterpieces which bequeathed upon us harmony.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:17.370
I wish to leave those which bring harmony to others.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.650
And, General Hashiba's orders?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.000
Milord requests ye to salvage the masterpieces of Sakamoto Castle.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.330
His order does naught but prolong the siege!

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:39.060
Also, I command none who may discern a masterpiece from dross!

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.270
However, I bring with me a warrior who may.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:46.830
Governor Furuta!

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.800
Governor Furuta Sasuke!

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.820
What shall ye have me do?

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:17.180
<b>June 14, 1582 {purple ts}</b>

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:17.180
<b>Yamashiro Province Ogurusu {ts}</b>

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:34.930
'Twas I who rebelled for the people, and desire naught but my head they do!

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.530
Milord!

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.230
How fare ye?!

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.660
'Twas lack of caution that I am injured.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.570
Why do ye not adorn these robes to avert the eyes of foes?!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.960
Now, adorn them and be of caution!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.440
We shan't.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.170
We desire Death to take us as warriors!

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:03.140
Elder, I desire not shelter for such men!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:06.680
Why assist men who burned Enryaku Temple
 and slaughtered our brethren?!

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:12.180
So long as we remain, unharmed we shan't be!

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:16.590
When Hashiba holds reigns, shall the past offenses of Enryaku Temple be pardoned?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:21.570
Uncertain of this, require we do an effective leader seasoned in warfare!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.900
Go, Milord!

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.590
I, Mizo Katsube, shall hold their pursuit!

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:45.020
Just, be my actions...?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.570
<b>June 14, 1582 {ts red}</b>

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.570
<b>Omi Province Sakamoto Castle {ts}</b>

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:06.580
'Tis the son-in-law of Mitsuhide, Akechi Hidemitsu!

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.620
General, shall we fire?

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.040
Hear me! {kikei}

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.120
Hold!

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.300
I have with me the masterpieces of Milord!

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:17.670
Before ye monkeys do unto them harm, we relinquish the masterpieces!

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:23.500
He dares to insult his foes before departing towards an honorable death?

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:26.230
A most admirable warrior.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.060
Governor Furuta!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.650
Fish the treasures from the river and thoroughly inspect them!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:38.780
Governor!

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:47.310
As you wish.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:59.340
A tubicle ewer,

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.170
a celadon gourd flower vase,

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.880
a laurel tea jar,

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.820
a large autumn jar,

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.310
and a Tenmoku-glazed frost tea bowl.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:18.470
No matter the masterpieces I behold here, not a single article piques my interest.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:21.250
The reason is known to me.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:28.080
My lust of masterpieces be akin to my admiration for Milord.

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:35.290
Adorned I had a veil, lusting for masterpieces, in belief that I may ascend to lord as Milord had. {until omotteitanoda}

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:39.830
With the passing of Milord

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.250
and the identity of his assassin known to me,

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.340
the veil be rendered to mere cloth.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:53.570
That which mine eyes desire...

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.270
and that which mine heart yearns for...

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:15.420
A nameless earth ware of yore!

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.500
The lure of this ware be that of its stout, yet imperfect form!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:28.140
Master Soueki, be this a ware of virtue in your philosophy of imperfection?

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.140
Survived many an era buried under rock and stone to be unearthed.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:38.900
Were masterpieces representations of men who dare to grasp the title of lord...

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.190
perhaps this represents mineself?

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.710
That a masterpiece?

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:51.740
General Akechi retains foul wares, he does!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:52.660
You cur!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.050
Insult not my pride!

00:14:57.030 --> 00:15:01.470
Then I shall retain this article.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:06.810
I daren't present a foul ware to General Hashiba.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:12.220
Be that baldy...

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.890
Insult Milord, aye?

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.160
I serve Milord Oda Nobunaga!

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:22.380
To insult Milord is to insult me!

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.970
Give me the last ware!

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.950
G-General, must we relinquish the Octagonal Kettle-?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.210
B-Be of care...! {t-teichou ni}

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.790
Go forth!

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.430
Joyous am I!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.950
Now, I may ascend to Nirvana content!

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:18.820
S-Sakamoto Castle burns... {until sakamoto jou ga}

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.410
We make haste!

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.840
Ye've not the leisure to shed tears!

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:37.800
Men approach.

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:54.360
They be warriors of Enryaku Temple!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.320
Brothers, my gratitude to ye.

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:02.370
Such escort ensures General Akechi safe-!

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.250
Identify yourselves!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.930
My fellow elders of Enryaku Temple be fools to approach a foe of the Buddha. {until wakaran no da}

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:45.070
Know the wrath of our slaughtered brethren to men of Oda Nobunaga...!

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:56.880
Milord!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.770
General, ye shielded from me the blade...!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:10.130
W-We must halt the bleeding!

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.490
Monk, what name have ye...?

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:20.780
I am Zuifu.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:24.200
Milord, speak naught!

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:28.980
Content am I...

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.800
that my last act saved the life of an innocent.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.050
We near the steppes of Enryaku Temple! {until ni gozaimasu}

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.680
This act shan't be your last...!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.950
It shan't be!

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:06.480
The smoke of Sakamoto Castle appears as kettle steam, fleeting in the autumn wind. {until yuge no you da}

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:10.900
Master Senno...

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:17.950
I am now a sage of imperfection.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:25.450
As I pass, prefer I do a life of aesthetics...

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:34.020
Had I only lived as Governor Furuta...

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.350
General Akechi!

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.690
Be conscious, Milord! {o ki wo tashika akechi sama}

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:58.140
Forgive the burdens I've done unto ye, Hiroko.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:02.230
Require a long respite, we both...

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:13.050
Under the crescent...

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:20.320
Akechi beckons his wife... {until hanashisemu}

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:24.670
What of the final verse?!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:26.100
Milord, be conscious!

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.510
I require the final verse! {until yomu no desu}

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.010
'Tis not a poem without it!

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:46.190
My passing needs no final verse...

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:14.270
Milord! {for both akechi samas}

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:21.150
I ask your pardon before execution, my fellow.

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:30.160
Executions unto any and all make ye akin to Oda Nobunaga!

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:32.010
Hold your tongue!

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:37.660
<b>'Tis ambition {red ts}</b>

00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:43.630
<b>I detest this cloth {purple ts}</b>

00:24:48.460 --> 00:24:50.130
<b>Ye lent a hand, no? {blue ts}</b>

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:53.080
The Times are A-changing.

00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:58.390
Does the fork joining the aesthete and warrior exist?

00:24:56.550 --> 00:24:59.920
<b>The Times are A-changing{ts}</b>
